import{as as e,c as n,ar as i,x as t,y as o,B as a,O as s}from"./b2c89b892.js";const r={class:"page-doc"},l={class:"title"},c=["innerHTML"],d={__name:"Doc",props:{type:{type:String,default:""}},setup(d){const u=d,{t:h}=e(),p=i(),m={yhxy:{title:h("pc.yonghuxieyi"),info:'Welcome to this website and related services (hereinafter referred to as "this website"). Before accessing or using this website, please carefully read and fully understand this User Agreement (hereinafter referred to as "this Agreement"). By accessing, browsing, registering, or using this website, you indicate that you have read, understood, and agreed to all the terms and conditions of this Agreement.\n\nI. Scope of Application\n\nThis Agreement applies to all users who access or use this website (hereinafter referred to as "User" or "you").\n\nThis Agreement stipulates the rights and obligations between the User and the website operator (hereinafter referred to as "we" or "the website provider") when using the services of this website.\n\nIf a User does not agree to any content of this Agreement, they should immediately stop accessing or using this website.\n\nII. Website Usage Rules\n\nUsers shall comply with the laws and regulations of their locality and the relevant regulations of this website, and shall not use this website to engage in any illegal or improper activities.\n\nUsers promise not to access or interfere with the normal operation of this website through any automated programs, scripts, crawlers, etc.\n\nUsers shall bear legal responsibility for all their actions on this website (including filling in information, uploading files, commenting, etc.).\n\nThe website operator reserves the right to modify, suspend, or terminate website services at any time based on actual circumstances without prior notice to users.\n\nIII. Information and Content Description\n\nThe content provided on this website (including text, images, audio, video, data, charts, etc.) is for general informational purposes only and does not constitute any legal, investment, financial, or other professional advice.\n\nThe website operator strives to ensure the accuracy and timeliness of the information provided, but does not guarantee the completeness or applicability of the information.\n\nUsers should make their own judgments and bear the risks before making any decisions based on the information on this website.\n\nIV. Intellectual Property Statement\n\nAll content, structure, page design, source code, trademarks, and logos on this website are protected by intellectual property laws.\n\nWithout authorization, no entity or individual may copy, reproduce, modify, disseminate, publish, display, or otherwise use the content of this website.\n\nThe website operator reserves the right to pursue legal action against any violation of this clause.\n\nV. Privacy and Data Protection\n\nThe website operator values ​​user privacy and will protect users\' personal information in accordance with applicable laws and the Privacy Policy.\n\nInformation provided by users during their use of this website will only be used for service provision, communication, and other purposes required by law.\n\nThe website will not sell, rent, or disclose users\' personal information without authorization.\n\nVI. Account and Security\n\nIf the website provides registration services, users should safeguard their login name and password and must not transfer or lend their account to others.\n\nUsers are responsible for all actions taken using their accounts. If unauthorized use of the account is discovered, the user should immediately notify the website.\n\nThe website has the right to suspend or terminate a user\'s account for security or administrative needs.\n\nVII. Disclaimer and Limitation of Liability\n\nUsers understand and agree that the website is not liable for the following:\n\nLosses caused by the use or inability to use the website\'s services;\n\nLosses caused by third-party causes (including but not limited to network failures, viruses, and hacker attacks);\n\nLosses caused by the user\'s own actions (such as operational errors, information leaks, etc.).\n\nThe website does not guarantee that the website will be uninterrupted or error-free, nor does it guarantee that defects will be promptly fixed.\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, the website operator\'s total liability to the user shall not exceed the fees paid by the user for using this website (if any).\n\nVIII. Amendment and Termination of Agreement\n\nThe website operator reserves the right to amend, update, or terminate this agreement at any time. The amended agreement shall take effect upon publication.\n\nContinue access to or use of this website constitutes acceptance of the amended terms.\n\nUsers may terminate this agreement by ceasing use of this website at any time.\n\nIX. Governing Law and Dispute Resolution\n\nThe formation, performance, and interpretation of this agreement shall be governed by the laws of the location of the website operator.\n\nAny dispute arising from this agreement shall be settled amicably through negotiation between the parties; if the negotiation fails, either party may bring suit in a court with jurisdiction in the location of the website operator.'},yszc:{title:h("gongyong.yinsizhengce"),info:"This Privacy Policy (“Policy”) applies to your access and use of this website and related services (“the Site”).\nWe value your privacy and are committed to protecting your personal information in accordance with applicable data protection laws and regulations. Please read this Policy carefully to understand how we collect, use, store, and safeguard your information.\n \n1. Information We Collect\n \nWe may collect personal information in the following ways:\n \nInformation You Provide Voluntarily\nWhen you register an account, fill out forms, subscribe to newsletters, contact customer service, or participate in events, you may provide information such as your name, email address, phone number, and company name.\n \nInformation Collected Automatically\nWhen you visit our website, we may automatically collect certain data including your IP address, browser type, device model, access time, pages visited, and cookie information.\n \nInformation from Third Parties\nWhere permitted by law, we may receive supplementary information about you from business partners or public sources to improve our services or verify your identity.\n \n2. How We Use Information\n \nWe may use the collected information for the following purposes:\n \nTo provide, maintain, and improve our website and related services;\n \nTo communicate with you and respond to inquiries;\n \nTo send updates, newsletters, promotional materials, or other communications (you may opt out at any time);\n \nTo perform analytics and improve site performance;\n \nTo comply with legal obligations and prevent fraud or misuse.\n \n3. Cookies and Tracking Technologies\n \nWe use cookies and similar technologies (such as web beacons and pixels) to enhance user experience, analyze site traffic, and personalize content.\n \nYou may disable cookies through your browser settings; however, some features of the site may not function properly as a result.\n \nWe may use third-party analytics tools (e.g., Google Analytics) to better understand user behavior, which may collect anonymized statistical information.\n \n4. Information Sharing and Disclosure\n \nWe do not sell or rent your personal information to unrelated third parties.\nWe may disclose your information only in the following cases:\n \nWith your explicit consent or authorization;\n \nTo comply with applicable laws, regulations, or governmental requests;\n \nTo protect our legal rights or prevent fraud and security threats;\n \nTo trusted third-party service providers (e.g., payment processors, hosting, email delivery) who assist us in operating our business and are bound by confidentiality obligations.\n \n5. Information Storage and Security\n \nWe adopt industry-standard security measures, including encryption, access control, and firewalls, to protect your data.\n \nPersonal data is stored on secure servers accessible only to authorized personnel.\n \nHowever, please note that no method of internet transmission or electronic storage is 100% secure; you acknowledge and accept the inherent risks of data transmission online.\n \n6. Data Retention\n \nWe retain personal information for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this Policy, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law.\nOnce data is no longer needed, we will delete or anonymize it securely.\n \n7. Your Rights\n \nDepending on applicable laws, you may have the following rights regarding your personal information:\n \nThe right to access and obtain a copy of your data;\n \nThe right to request correction, update, or deletion of your data;\n \nThe right to withdraw consent or restrict certain processing activities;\n \nThe right to request data portability where applicable.\n \nIf you wish to exercise these rights, please contact us using the details provided in the “Contact Us” section. We will respond within a reasonable timeframe.\n \n8. Children’s Privacy\n \nOur website and services are not directed toward individuals under the age of 16.\nIf we become aware that we have collected personal data from a minor without parental consent, we will take immediate steps to delete such information.\n \n9. International Data Transfers\n \nYour information may be transferred to and processed in other countries or regions where data protection laws may differ from those of your jurisdiction.\nWe will take appropriate safeguards to ensure that your information remains protected.\n \n10. Policy Updates\n \nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect legal or operational changes.\nThe updated version will be posted on this page with a new “Last Updated” date.\nBy continuing to use the site after updates are posted, you agree to the revised Policy.\n"},flzr:{title:h("coinbase.falvzeren"),info:'Please read the following terms and conditions carefully. By accessing this website, you agree to and accept all terms and conditions.\n\n1. General Information and Non-Advice Nature\nAll content, information, data, and materials provided on this website are for general informational purposes only.\n\nNon-Investment Advice: Nothing on this website (including any market analysis, commentary, or discussion) should be considered personalized investment advice, tax advice, legal advice, or accounting advice for any specific individual.\n\nNon-Offer or Solicitation: The information on this website does not constitute an offer, solicitation, or recommendation to buy or sell any securities, investment products, or services.\n\nProfessional Advice: Before making any investment decision, you must consult a licensed professional advisor to consider your specific financial situation, investment objectives, and risk tolerance.\n\n2. Accuracy and "As Is" Provision\nThis company (or the operator of this website) strives to ensure the accuracy and timeliness of the information on the website, but does not guarantee the completeness, accuracy, or continued availability of the information.\n\nLimitation of Liability: This website and all its content are provided "as is" without any express or implied warranties of any kind.\n\nUpdate: Website information is subject to change without notice. We have no obligation to update or correct outdated information.\n\n3. Historical Performance and Forward-Looking Statements\n\nHistorical Performance: Any historical investment performance or metrics mentioned do not guarantee future results, nor do they indicate or guarantee a return on any particular investment. Investing involves risk, and you may lose your principal.\n\nForward-Looking Statements: Forward-looking statements (if any) on this website are based on current expectations and involve known and unknown risks and uncertainties. Actual results may differ materially from projections.\n\n4. Third-Party Content and Links\nThis website may contain links to third-party websites or content provided by third parties.\n\nNo Endorsement: We are not responsible for the content, services, products, or privacy policies of any third-party websites. Providing links does not constitute an endorsement, approval, or recommendation of that third party or its content.\n\nRisk: You assume all risk when accessing any third-party links and using their content.\n\n5. Legal and Regulatory Restrictions\nOur products and services are not available in all jurisdictions. Information on this website is intended only for users in jurisdictions where use and distribution will not violate local laws or regulations.\n\nCompliance: You are responsible for complying with all applicable laws and regulations in your jurisdiction.\n\n6. Limitation of Liability: To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Company and its affiliates, directors, officers, employees, and agents shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages (including, without limitation, loss of profits, business interruption, or loss of data) arising out of or in connection with the use of or inability to use this website and its content, even if the Company has been advised of the possibility of such damages.'},fxqzc:{title:h("coinbase.fanxiqianzhengce"),info:"This Anti-Money Laundering (AML) Policy (“Policy”) outlines the commitment of our organization (“the Company,” “we,” or “us”) to prevent and detect any form of money laundering, terrorist financing, or related illegal activity.\nWe operate in full compliance with applicable anti-money laundering and counter-terrorist financing laws and regulations, including the U.S. Bank Secrecy Act (BSA), the USA PATRIOT Act, and the guidelines established by the Financial Crimes Enforcement Network (FinCEN) and the Financial Action Task Force (FATF).\n\n1. Purpose\n\nThe purpose of this Policy is to establish effective internal controls, procedures, and training designed to:\n\nPrevent the Company and its clients from being used to facilitate money laundering or terrorist financing;\n\nDetect and report suspicious activities in a timely manner;\n\nEnsure full compliance with all relevant AML/CFT obligations.\n\n2. Scope\n\nThis Policy applies to all employees, officers, consultants, contractors, and affiliates of the Company, as well as any individuals or entities engaging in business with us.\nAll persons covered by this Policy must adhere to its principles, regardless of geographic location.\n\n3. Definition of Money Laundering\n\nMoney laundering refers to any process by which individuals or entities attempt to conceal or disguise the origin of funds derived from illegal activities, typically by transferring them through legitimate financial channels.\nThis may include:\n\nPlacement of illicit funds into the financial system;\n\nLayering through complex transactions to obscure their source;\n\nIntegration of “cleaned” funds back into the economy as legitimate assets.\n\n4. Customer Due Diligence (CDD)\n\nWe conduct Customer Due Diligence (CDD) and, where appropriate, Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) before establishing any client relationship. This includes:\n\nIdentity Verification – Obtaining and verifying official identification documents such as government-issued IDs, passports, or corporate registration certificates;\n\nBeneficial Ownership Identification – Identifying and verifying the ultimate beneficial owners of client accounts or entities;\n\nOngoing Monitoring – Continuously reviewing transactions for unusual or suspicious patterns;\n\nRisk Assessment – Assigning a risk profile to each client based on factors such as geography, business type, and transaction volume.\n\n5. Record Keeping\n\nAll records relating to client identification, account activity, and transaction history are securely maintained for a minimum of five (5) years after the end of the client relationship, or longer as required by applicable law.\nRecords are kept in a manner that allows prompt retrieval for regulatory review.\n\n6. Monitoring and Reporting\n\nAll transactions are monitored using risk-based systems to identify suspicious activities.\n\nAny employee who detects unusual or potentially suspicious behavior must immediately report it to the Company’s Compliance Officer.\n\nThe Compliance Officer is responsible for filing Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs) or equivalent notifications to the relevant authorities (e.g., FinCEN) when appropriate.\n\nWe maintain strict confidentiality regarding all reports and client information, consistent with applicable legal requirements.\n\n7. Training and Awareness\n\nAll employees receive regular AML training that includes:\n\nRecognizing red flags and typologies of money laundering;\n\nUnderstanding the Company’s CDD and reporting procedures;\n\nLearning the consequences of non-compliance with AML regulations.\n\nTraining is mandatory upon hiring and refreshed periodically.\n\n8. Independent Audit and Compliance Oversight\n\nThe Company conducts periodic independent reviews of its AML program to ensure its effectiveness, adequacy, and compliance with regulatory requirements.\nThe Compliance Officer is responsible for maintaining ongoing oversight and promptly implementing any recommended improvements.\n\n9. Sanctions Compliance\n\nThe Company strictly adheres to all applicable international sanctions programs, including those administered by the U.S. Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC), the United Nations, and the European Union.\nWe do not engage in business with individuals, entities, or countries subject to economic or trade sanctions.\n\n10. Responsibilities\n\nEvery employee is required to:\n\nFollow the Company’s AML procedures and controls;\n\nImmediately report suspicious activity to the Compliance Officer;\n\nCooperate fully with internal or regulatory investigations.\n\nFailure to comply with this Policy may result in disciplinary action, termination, or legal penalties.\n\n11. Review and Updates\n\nThis Policy is reviewed at least annually, or whenever there are significant changes in applicable laws or the Company’s operations.\nThe updated version will be published on our official website and made available to all employees and partners."}},y=n(()=>m[u.type||p.query.type]||{});return(e,n)=>(o(),t("div",r,[a("div",l,s(y.value.title),1),a("pre",{class:"info",innerHTML:y.value.info},null,8,c)]))}};export{d as default};
